{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/988152-has-anyone-played-mummy","id":988152,"title":"Has anyone played Mummy?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-15T23:29:21-07:00","id":988152,"title":"Has anyone played Mummy?","content":"I got the PDFs off of DTRpg and they're pretty interesting to read but How is the game in play?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10304-rester","name":"Rester","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T01:15:57-07:00","id":988178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rester</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/988152-has-anyone-played-mummy#post988152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got the PDFs off of DTRpg and they're pretty interesting to read but How is the game in play?</div> </div> </div> </div>Which edition? MTR is pretty much a completely different game, and defaults to the thing in CTD and DTF where you're actually a modern human but with a (bit of) supernatural soul. <br /> <br /> In older versions, you played a millennia-old undead sorcerer, so the game was a much more accurate evocation of mummy myths. MTR was more low-powered Middle Eastern supers than it was ancient, cursed Egyptian lords. I like both, but for very different reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T04:44:02-07:00","id":988208,"title":"","content":"In MTR there are more ways to terminate ultimately a mummy, and more background, but it breaks the dark-gothic style of WoD because they are a light of faith and hope.<br /> <br /> You can kill a mummy, but it only mades her get furious even more. <br /> <br /> The mummies are too powerful to be only unknown suporting actors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T09:35:52-07:00","id":988280,"title":"","content":"We test drove the game back when the full-on Mummy the Resurrection came out. Just a mini-mini-chronicle of one one story of three or so sessions, with a few players from the usual bunch. It was amazing how insanely powerful a starting mummy could be. One character was able to change the weather over a pretty significant area (like a chunk of a hemisphere) with a really good roll.<br /> <br /> It was fun. It never made it to a full-on game. Probably a mini-chronicle of several months. I think, overall, we would have had more fun with longer running Hunter the Reckoing game. But... not unfun at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T19:21:57-07:00","id":990211,"title":"","content":"I have all three editions plus the Resurrection Player's Guide. It is very surprising to see how much the game changed overtime. the thing that got me the most about Resurrection was that it felt so much like a NWOD/ChroD game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10304-rester","name":"Rester","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}